Description: proof-of-work HTTP proxy that challenges scraper bots
 Anubis is a reverse proxy that weighs incoming HTTP requests against a
 policy of rules (user agent, path, address ranges, expressions) and,
 for the requests that look like automated scrapers, answers with a
 challenge page whose JavaScript proof of work a browser solves once
 before it receives a signed cookie and reaches the protected site.
 .
 The built-in policy allows the major search engine crawlers only from
 their published address ranges and challenges anything else that
 claims to be a browser.
 .
 This package ships the anubis binary, anubis-robots2policy, a systemd
 template unit anubis@.service (one instance per environment file in
 /etc/anubis, disabled by default) and the default policy.
